# UI, Tailwind, and components

## Tailwind

- Obey ESLint **`tailwindcss/classnames-order`** and **`enforces-shorthand`**—the build fails if classes are out of order or non-shorthand where shorthand applies.
- Prefer **`classnames`** / **`tailwind-merge`** patterns already used in components like modals and layout.

## Libraries

- Use **`@epam/ai-dial-ui-kit`** and related DIAL packages consistently with neighboring imports—do not duplicate design tokens or components the kit already provides.
- Icons often come from **`@tabler/icons-react`**—match existing icon choice and sizing.

## Accessibility and UX

- Preserve keyboard focus behavior where **`@floating-ui/react`** or similar patterns are used (see existing modal/dialog code).
- Maintain visible loading and empty states consistent with sibling tables, graphs, and chat panels.

## Assets and global styles

- Global styles live under **`src/app`** (`globals.css` and route-group imports)—avoid scattering global CSS from random feature folders unless that is the established pattern nearby.
